---
/*
 * Invite — the closing CTA: what signing up costs, and how you get in before it opens.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * THE HEADING WAS FALSE-IN-WAITING. "There is no signup yet." IS DEAD.
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * Kept here so nobody re-derives it from the git history. It was written when the endpoint
 * genuinely did not exist. It does now: `create_workspace` is handled by
 * createSelfServeWorkspace() in supabase/functions/command/index.ts, dispatched ahead of
 * route resolution because a brand-new caller has no membership to resolve against. What is
 * true today is that sign-up is GATED, not absent — and "gated" is a fact that survives
 * launch day, where "there is none" would have had to be found and rewritten.
 *
 * THIS CARD IS SPLIT DOWN THE MIDDLE ON PURPOSE, AND THE SPLIT IS THE POINT:
 *
 *   LEFT — heading, lede, facts. Permanent terms only. Every sentence there is true today
 *          AND on the day SWARM_SELF_SERVE flips to "1". Nothing on that side says "yet",
 *          "soon", or "not live", so nothing on that side rots.
 *   RIGHT — the invite form. This is the only part that speaks about today, because it is
 *          also the only part that has to be rewritten when the endpoint is reachable. Put
 *          temporal copy here or nowhere.
 *
 * WHERE THE LEFT-HAND FACTS WERE CHECKED, all in supabase/functions/command/index.ts:
 *   3 live workspaces .... FREE_TIER_WORKSPACE_LIMIT = 3 (:330), counted against rows with
 *                          archived_at IS NULL (:2245-2251) — archiving one frees the slot,
 *                          which is why the row says "live" and not just "three".
 *   verified identity .... a non-human credential is refused, then an unverified one
 *                          (:2183-2186); identityVerified is email_confirmed_at (:3205).
 *   no card .............. no billing surface exists in this repo. Enumerated with a control:
 *                          stripe|billing|payment|subscription|invoice|\bprice\b over src/,
 *                          supabase/functions/, supabase/migrations/ and package.json is 0
 *                          hits; "workspace" over the same paths is 1002, so the grep runs.
 *   GitHub sign-in ....... the front door on /start, and the OAuth the CLI already uses
 *                          (`cswarm login`, GitHub + PKCE — docs/marketing/SITE-BRIEF.md).
 *                          NOT VERIFIED: no provider is enabled in supabase/config.toml, so
 *                          this names the flow we ship, not a wired integration.
 *
 * NOTHING HERE SAYS SIGN-UP IS OPEN. It is not: the handler's first gate is
 * `SWARM_SELF_SERVE === "1"` (:323, :2182), unset in production, so an attempt today is a
 * 403. The form is what carries that, and it carries it once.
 *
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 *
 * THE SUBMIT PATH IS STILL A STUB, and it says so in three places a reader cannot miss —
 * all three now on the form side of the card, none of them in the heading:
 *
 *   1. the line under the form's title, before anything is typed;
 *   2. the field's own hint, which is read out with the control by a screen reader;
 *   3. the outcome after submitting, which reports exactly what happened — nothing.
 *
 * THREE MEANS THREE, and it did not used to. This card had shipped five: the heading, a
 * bolded clause in the lede ("a front end with nothing behind it"), the Access row's
 * "— not self-serve", a "Front end only" badge on the form title, and the hint — with the
 * outcome making six and the site footer a seventh 200px below. Measured on the built page,
 * the closing screenful restated the same fact eight times. Honesty was never the problem;
 * the volume was, and a page that says one thing eight times reads as apologising for
 * itself. The badge and the bolded clause went then; the heading went now, when it stopped
 * being true. Count stays at three: anything added here that restates the stub is a fourth
 * placement — put it in one of the three or leave it out.
 *
 * It NEVER shows a success state. A green tick reading "You're on the list!" over a form
 * with no backend is the single most common lie on a pre-launch page, and it is the one
 * thing this component is written to make impossible.
 *
 * WHY THE VALIDATION IS REAL ANYWAY. The parts that can be honest are: the field validates,
 * the error is a real error, and the outcome is the truth. That is a working front end
 * waiting for a server, which is what it actually is.
 *
 * WHY THERE IS NO SPINNER. Nothing is in flight. A loading state here would be a fabricated
 * latency invented to make a stub feel like a service.
 *
 * INTEGRATION CORRECTION: the Repository row read "Private while we dogfood". It is not.
 * Re-checked live: github.com/Ridge-io/cloud-swarm answers 200 to a logged-out request, with
 * a made-up repo path returning 404 as the control. The row now names and links the repo.
 * The same false claim was rendered by two of the site's three footers; those are deleted.
 *
 * FACTS: pre-launch, invited dogfood — docs/marketing/SITE-BRIEF.md. (Historical note, kept
 * because it explains the fix above: the repo WAS private, which is why nothing here linked
 * to it. The old note read: github.com/Ridge-io/cloud-swarm returns
 * 404 to a logged-out visitor). Licence MIT — package.json at the repo root.
 */

import Input from "../ui/Input.astro";
---

<section class="section section--tight invite" id="invite" aria-labelledby="invite-title">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="card card--lg card--raised invite__card js-reveal">
      <div class="invite__copy">
        {/* "Pricing", because that is what the list under it now answers. The eyebrow read
            "Status" while the rows below were access, licence and repo — a heading for a
            different table. */}
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing</p>
        <h2 class="h-section invite__title" id="invite-title">
          Free, and capped at three workspaces.
        </h2>
        <p class="lede invite__lede">
          Sign in with GitHub, name a workspace, bring your agents in. No card at any point.
        </p>

        <ul class="invite__facts">
          <li>
            <span class="invite__k">Free tier</span>
            <span class="invite__v">3 live workspaces per verified identity</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="invite__k">Sign-in</span>
            <span class="invite__v">GitHub</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="invite__k">Cost</span>
            <span class="invite__v">No card, no billing</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="invite__k">Shape</span>
            <span class="invite__v">A CLI and a hosted service</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="invite__k">Repository</span>
            <span class="invite__v">
              <a class="invite__a" href="https://github.com/Ridge-io/cloud-swarm" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
                Ridge-io/cloud-swarm<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span>
              </a>
            </span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="invite__k">Licence</span>
            <span class="invite__v">MIT</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <form class="invite__form" id="invite-form" novalidate>
        <h3 class="invite__form-title">
          Request an invite
        </h3>

        {/* Placement 1 of 3. The only sentence on this card that talks about today, and it
            is on the side of the card that has to be rewritten when the endpoint opens. */}
        <p class="invite__form-note">
          Self-serve signup is built and not switched on for everyone yet. Until it is,
          invitations come from someone who already has a workspace.
        </p>

        <Input
          id="invite-email"
          name="email"
          type="email"
          label="Email"
          placeholder="you@company.com"
          autocomplete="email"
          hint="Nothing is sent. There is no service behind this button yet."
        />
        <p class="invite__err" id="invite-email-err" hidden>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
            <path d="M12 7.5v5"></path>
            <path d="M12 16.2v.2"></path>
          </svg>
          <span id="invite-email-err-text">That does not look like an email address.</span>
        </p>

        <button class="btn btn--lg btn--primary btn--block" type="submit">
          Request an invite
        </button>

        {/* Server-rendered and empty, so the live region is registered before anything is
            put in it — a region created in the same tick as its content announces nothing. */}
        <div class="invite__out" id="invite-out" role="status" hidden>
          <p class="invite__out-title">Nothing was sent.</p>
          <p class="invite__out-body">
            That is not an error and you did not do anything wrong — this button has nothing
            behind it to receive an address. When it does, this is the button that will reach
            it. Until then, invitations come from someone who already has a workspace.
          </p>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  /* No network call is made here, and none is possible: there is nothing to call. The
     form’s only job is to validate honestly and then say what really happened. */
  const form = document.getElementById("invite-form") as HTMLFormElement | null;
  const field = document.getElementById("invite-email") as HTMLInputElement | null;
  const err = document.getElementById("invite-email-err");
  const errText = document.getElementById("invite-email-err-text");
  const out = document.getElementById("invite-out");

  if (form && field && err && errText && out) {
    const wrapper = field.closest(".ui-field");

    const setError = (message: string | null) => {
      err.hidden = message === null;
      if (message) errText.textContent = message;
      field.setAttribute("aria-invalid", message ? "true" : "false");
      field.setAttribute(
        "aria-describedby",
        message ? "invite-email-hint invite-email-err" : "invite-email-hint"
      );
      wrapper?.classList.toggle("ui-field--error", message !== null);
    };

    form.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const value = field.value.trim();

      if (!value) {
        out.hidden = true;
        setError("Enter an email address first.");
        field.focus();
        return;
      }
      /* Deliberately loose. Tight email regexes reject real addresses, and the only thing
         this check is for is catching an obvious typo before an honest dead end. */
      if (!/^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/.test(value)) {
        out.hidden = true;
        setError("That does not look like an email address.");
        field.focus();
        return;
      }

      setError(null);
      out.hidden = false;
    });

    field.addEventListener("input", () => {
      if (field.value.trim()) setError(null);
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  /* [hidden] is (0,1,0) in the UA sheet and any author rule of the same weight beats it.
     .invite__out and .invite__err are both flex, so without this they would never hide. */
  [hidden] {
    display: none !important;
  }

  /* center, not start: the facts list runs about twice the height of the form, and
     top-aligning left a column of nothing under the button inside the card. */
  .invite__card {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(var(--s-8), 5vw, var(--s-16));
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 56rem) {
    .invite__card {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }

  .invite__copy {
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  .invite .invite__title {
    font-size: var(--t-2xl);
    margin-block: var(--s-3) var(--stack-sm);
  }

  .invite__lede {
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    line-height: var(--lh-lg);
  }

  .invite__facts {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--s-8) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .invite__facts li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    padding-block: var(--s-3);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .invite__k {
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--track-eyebrow);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .invite__v {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    color: var(--text);
    text-align: end;
  }

  /* The Repository row is the one fact here that is also a place you can go. Monospace
     because it is a repo path, not prose. */
  .invite__a {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--t-xs);
    color: var(--text);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--border-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    transition: color var(--dur-2) var(--ease-standard),
      text-decoration-color var(--dur-2) var(--ease-standard);
  }

  .invite__a:hover {
    color: var(--accent-bright);
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }

  /* --- form --------------------------------------------------------------- */

  .invite__form {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    min-inline-size: 0;
    padding: var(--pad-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--elev-2);
  }

  .invite__form-title {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--t-lg);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    line-height: var(--lh-lg);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  /* Pulled up against the form title rather than sitting on the form's own --s-4 gap: it is
     a subhead for that title, not the next thing in the form. Same negative-margin trick
     .invite__err uses below, for the same reason. */
  .invite__form-note {
    margin-block-start: calc(var(--s-4) * -1 + var(--s-2));
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted); /* 7.03:1 on --elev-2, the form's surface */
  }

  .invite__err {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--s-2);
    margin-block-start: calc(var(--s-4) * -1 + var(--s-1));
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
    color: var(--danger);
  }

  .invite__err svg {
    inline-size: 1.05em;
    block-size: 1.05em;
    flex: none;
    margin-block-start: 0.2em;
  }

  /* Deliberately NOT success-coloured. This is an outcome, and the outcome is "nothing
     happened" — painting it green would be the lie this component exists to avoid. */
  .invite__out {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--stack-xs);
    padding: var(--pad-card-sm);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--elev-0);
    animation: invite-in var(--dur-3) var(--ease-decelerate) both;
  }

  @keyframes invite-in {
    from {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translate3d(0, 4px, 0);
    }
    to {
      opacity: 1;
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  .invite__out-title {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .invite__out-body {
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    line-height: var(--lh-sm);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
